@X0ATELNET
------
@X03Dependant on your operating system.


@X02OS/2
----
@X03Connect ethernet connection to Router.  Use SIO.SYS software as a serial
driver.  This software comes with a program called VModem which will
vitualize a com port.  This means that you can assign port 16 (any port
really) that doesn't exist, and any application can access it.  This port
is actually going through your network card.

PCBoard communicates with a virtual port which goes to the router through
an ethernet connection.  Ports are defined through SIO.SYS.  SIO.SYS is
available on Salt Air.  Filenames are:  @X0CSIO153.ZIP@X03,@X0C SIO155.ZIP@X03.


@X0D+--------+
| Basic  |
|Hardware|--> Ethernet network --> Ethernet Card --> Vmodem software
+--------+


